<code>assert index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))));</code>

This assert statement captures the essence of the comment by ensuring that for every valid index within the specified range, the element at position `i` after the removal is either `null` if the element at position `i+1` was `null`, or it equals the element at position `i+1` if it was not `null`.
